1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,040
Twenty-five centuries ago,

2
00:00:02,670 --> 00:00:04,190
a man named Zeno proved

3
00:00:04,230 --> 00:00:06,160
that nothing ever arrived.

4
00:00:06,661 --> 00:00:08,871
Hi. I am Jahan,

5
00:00:09,281 --> 00:00:11,691
and something impossible happened to me.

6
00:00:11,891 --> 00:00:12,521
Her.

7
00:00:14,897 --> 00:00:16,787
Zeno's argument is simple.

8
00:00:17,077 --> 00:00:18,327
To reach any place,

9
00:00:18,817 --> 00:00:20,867
you must first cover half the distance.

10
00:00:21,208 --> 00:00:22,838
Then half of what remains.

11
00:00:23,251 --> 00:00:24,661
Then half of that.

12
00:00:24,934 --> 00:00:26,804
The halves never run out.

13
00:00:27,038 --> 00:00:28,668
There is always a remainder,

14
00:00:29,138 --> 00:00:31,248
and the remainder has a remainder,

15
00:00:31,598 --> 00:00:33,898
so the traveller is stranded forever

16
00:00:33,938 --> 00:00:36,088
in the generous middle of the road.

17
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:38,450
For centuries, this

18
00:00:38,490 --> 00:00:40,820
was treated as a puzzle about motion.

19
00:00:41,113 --> 00:00:43,663
I submit it is a puzzle about waiting.

20
00:00:44,638 --> 00:00:45,928
Here is the evidence.

21
00:00:46,349 --> 00:00:47,159
A gate.

22
00:00:47,477 --> 00:00:48,347
A street.

23
00:00:48,704 --> 00:00:50,534
Eleven metres of tarmac.

24
00:00:50,813 --> 00:00:52,463
The hazard lights ticking.

25
00:00:53,397 --> 00:00:54,357
And you, still

26
00:00:54,397 --> 00:00:56,087
somewhere in the first half,

27
00:00:56,377 --> 00:00:57,647
which makes you,

28
00:00:57,877 --> 00:01:01,087
by every known law of logic, impossible.

29
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:04,010
I have watched this hundreds of times.

30
00:01:05,175 --> 00:01:08,125
Mathematicians eventually rescued us.

31
00:01:08,324 --> 00:01:09,834
Add every half together,

32
00:01:09,904 --> 00:01:12,114
they said: a half,

33
00:01:12,164 --> 00:01:13,814
a quarter, an eighth,

34
00:01:14,224 --> 00:01:16,194
and the total is exactly one.

35
00:01:16,730 --> 00:01:19,440
The infinite fits inside a finite walk.

36
00:01:19,623 --> 00:01:20,773
How reassuring.

37
00:01:21,630 --> 00:01:24,000
But the sum only measures how far.

38
00:01:24,211 --> 00:01:24,971
It cannot say

39
00:01:25,011 --> 00:01:26,721
what the in-between is like:

40
00:01:26,890 --> 00:01:28,030
the hair in your face

41
00:01:28,070 --> 00:01:29,360
at the quarter mark,

42
00:01:29,910 --> 00:01:31,350
the half-smile you wear

43
00:01:31,390 --> 00:01:33,420
when you think nobody's watching.

44
00:01:34,842 --> 00:01:36,842
Heraclitus said no one steps

45
00:01:36,882 --> 00:01:38,552
into the same river twice.

46
00:01:38,888 --> 00:01:40,328
Nobody gets into the same

47
00:01:40,368 --> 00:01:42,138
car twice, either.

48
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:43,810
Hundred arrivals,

49
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,730
hundred different women,

50
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:47,970
and every single one of them you.

51
00:01:52,478 --> 00:01:54,398
Diogenes answered Zeno

52
00:01:54,438 --> 00:01:56,128
by standing up and walking.

53
00:01:56,378 --> 00:01:59,128
You answer him every time by getting in.

54
00:02:00,208 --> 00:02:01,958
Love is not the proof.

55
00:02:03,398 --> 00:02:05,028
Love is the practical,

56
00:02:05,798 --> 00:02:06,968
slightly awkward,

57
00:02:07,118 --> 00:02:08,538
repeated action of putting

58
00:02:08,578 --> 00:02:10,978
the hazards on and sitting there

59
00:02:11,018 --> 00:02:12,878
while she crosses the distance

60
00:02:12,918 --> 00:02:15,748
that logic says can never be finished.

61
00:02:16,709 --> 00:02:17,819
I am here.

62
00:02:18,374 --> 00:02:19,444
No hurry.
